# Python
backend/.venv/
backend/__pycache__/
backend/**/__pycache__/
backend/**/*.pyc
backend/.env
backend/staticfiles/
backend/media/
backend/db.sqlite3

# Node
node_modules/
apps/*/node_modules/
packages/*/node_modules/

# Next.js
apps/*/.next/
apps/*/out/
# `vercel link`/`vercel pull` scratch state, including project.json — machine
# local, and it names the org and project ids.
.vercel/

# Env
#
# Blanket-ignore every .env file, at any depth, so a new one holding secrets
# cannot be committed by an absent-minded `git add .` — the repo is public.
# `.env.prod` and `backend/.env.prod` land here: they hold the production
# secrets read by infrastructure/docker/docker-compose.prod.yml.
.env*

# Then re-admit the two kinds that are public on purpose. These negations must
# stay below the blanket above — for a given path the last matching rule wins.
#
# The *.example templates document which variables exist and carry placeholder
# values, never real ones.
!.env*.example
# apps/web/.env.production holds the *public* half of the browser bundle's
# config, committed deliberately: next.config.ts inlines these values into
# JavaScript served to every visitor, and a build without them ships
# apiKey:"" plus a localhost API base. The file's own header says what may and
# may not go in it; read it before adding a line there.
!apps/web/.env.production
# TLS material mounted into the nginx container.
infrastructure/docker/certs/
# certbot's own state, created on the server by
# infrastructure/aws/setup-letsencrypt.sh. live/<domain>/privkey.pem is the
# certificate's private key, so this must never be committed — the repo is public.
infrastructure/docker/letsencrypt/
# Written on the server by the deploy, next to the checkout. The repo is public,
# so an admin password one `git add .` away from a commit is not a risk worth
# carrying.
.superuser-credentials

# Build artifacts
dist/
build/
# tsc's incremental cache. Tracked until now, which meant every `typecheck` run
# showed up as a modified file and one got committed as "Fixed" (14917ac).
*.tsbuildinfo

